# PML-004 — Configuration Management Standard

**Project:** Trading Intelligence Platform (TIP)
**Document ID:** PML-004
**Version:** 1.0.0
**Status:** Approved (Initial Baseline)
**Classification:** Project Governing Standard
**Owner:** TIP Architecture & Engineering Team
**Effective Date:** 2026-08-08

---

# 1. Purpose

The Configuration Management (CM) Standard establishes the policies, processes, and controls required to identify, version, manage, protect, and audit all configuration items (CIs) associated with the Trading Intelligence Platform (TIP).

Configuration Management ensures that the project remains reproducible, traceable, and maintainable throughout its lifecycle by controlling changes to software, documentation, infrastructure, databases, environments, and releases.

---

# 2. Scope

This standard applies to every configuration item created or maintained within the Trading Intelligence Platform, including:

* Source code
* Documentation
* Project Master Library (PML)
* Architecture Decision Records (ADR)
* Database schemas
* SQL migration scripts
* Configuration files
* Build scripts
* CI/CD pipelines
* Docker files
* Infrastructure definitions
* Test assets
* Release packages
* Deployment scripts

No controlled configuration item shall exist outside the approved repository structure.

---

# 3. Configuration Management Objectives

Configuration Management shall:

* Ensure every configuration item is uniquely identifiable.
* Maintain complete version history.
* Enable reproducible builds.
* Preserve release integrity.
* Support auditing and traceability.
* Prevent uncontrolled changes.
* Support rollback and disaster recovery.
* Maintain consistency across environments.

---

# 4. Configuration Item (CI) Definition

A Configuration Item (CI) is any artefact whose state must be controlled.

Examples include:

| CI Category    | Examples                               |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Documentation  | PML, Volumes 1–4, ADRs                 |
| Source Code    | MQL5, Python                           |
| Database       | Schema, migrations, seed data          |
| Infrastructure | Docker, deployment scripts             |
| Configuration  | JSON, YAML, INI, environment variables |
| Testing        | Test suites, test data                 |
| Release        | Packages, installers, binaries         |

Every CI shall have a unique identifier and version.

